Sets the two scores directly, as a precondition. The win and deuce rules still
resolve through real play, so a match ends when a real point is driven.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
### `setPaddle(side, patch)`
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
### `setPaddle(state, side, patch)`
{{else}}
### `setPaddle(side, patch)`
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq engine.slug "structured-2d")}}
Poses or moves a paddle. `side` is `"left"` or `"right"`; `patch` may set `cy`
(center y) and `vy` (vertical velocity in units per second). A `vy` set here is
written to the paddle and held by the driver for that side, so it persists across
frames and the paddle is still moving when it strikes the ball, which is what
drives the spin mechanic.
{{else}}
Poses or moves a paddle. `side` is `"left"` or `"right"`; `patch` may set `cy`
(center y) and `vy` (vertical velocity in units per second). A `vy` set here is
written to both the paddle and `driver.vy[side]`, so it persists across frames and
the paddle is still moving when it strikes the ball, which is what drives the spin
mechanic.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
### `setBall(index, patch)`
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
### `setBall(state, index, patch)`
{{else}}
### `setBall(index, patch)`
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq variant.slug "multi")}}
Places and aims a ball. `index` selects one of the three balls, numbered in play
order from `0`. `patch` may set any of `x`, `y`, `vx`, `vy`, and `spin`. Posing a
ball takes it into live play, clearing `held` and its hold timer, so a scenario
can drive one ball while parking the others out of the way.
{{else}}
Places and aims a ball. `index` is `0`, selecting the single ball in play. `patch`
may set any of `x`, `y`, `vx`, `vy`, and `spin`.
{{/if}}

